    <mxCell id="key" value="&lt;b&gt;Template deviation&lt;/b&gt;   the TDD template asks for a class diagram. This change set adds no classes, no interfaces and no runtime objects; its deliverables are markdown plus one script. The nearest honest artefact is this file-level dependency graph, and the deviation is recorded in TDD appendix B.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Edges&lt;/b&gt;   1  one authority text instantiates 27 copies · 2  baseline + exclusions are consumed by the validator, never by the instances · 3  the validator reads every instance root · 4  the only existing generation edge (conversions → extension resources) · 5  report is written once per run · 6  the markdown rendering is derived from the same model, never re-scanned&#10;&lt;b&gt;Direction rule&lt;/b&gt;   arrows point from producer to consumer. A back-arrow would mean an instance is normative — that is precisely the OI-05 defect this ticket removes." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#999999;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="840" y="440" width="290" height="250" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
